      "knownFor": "A Kzinti captain and commander of the Traitor's Claw in The Slaver Weapon, voiced by James Doohan.",
      "reveal": "The frozen role source names James Doohan in the actor field and states that the voice of Chuft-Captain was provided by him, supporting a voice-only performance claim for Chuft-Captain in The Slaver Weapon (1973). The same frozen role source says the rank rendered as part of Chuft-Captain's name follows Kzinti naming conventions devised by Kzinti creator Larry Niven; the frozen episode source credits Niven as writer and identifies the episode as adapted from his story The Soft Weapon, supporting a bounded writer / Kzinti naming convention credit. Cadmar, Cheeron, Domar, and Ari bn Bem remain separate roles. The exact role-specific still is retained as character evidence, while a separately sourced public-domain 1997 portrait supports Doohan's identity. No physical performance, animation, visual character design, voice direction, editing, sound processing, vocal transformation, production-shop, or other maker credit is inferred.",
